1
00:00:16,588 --> 00:00:20,027
[Korea]

2
00:00:20,027 --> 00:00:21,744
[Seoul, South Korea]

3
00:00:22,442 --> 00:00:25,715
[Ki Eunse is in yet another meeting today]

4
00:00:25,715 --> 00:00:28,215
[1st generation influencer & actress, Ki Eunse]

5
00:00:29,192 --> 00:00:30,309
[Knocking]

6
00:00:30,958 --> 00:00:32,825
[What brand is today's meeting for?]

7
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:35,253
[Kkang Stylist?] - Hello.
- Welcome.

8
00:00:35,253 --> 00:00:37,405
Hello, will this fit in here?

9
00:00:37,405 --> 00:00:39,723
[Make the impossible possible]
I'm a fashion creator from Korea.

10
00:00:39,723 --> 00:00:43,761
I also run fashion brands
and a fashion platform.

11
00:00:43,761 --> 00:00:46,563
[Fashion influencer with 20 billion won sales]
I'm Kang Daeheon, Kkang Stylist.

12
00:00:46,563 --> 00:00:49,019
I was the first in Korea

13
00:00:49,019 --> 00:00:52,522
to become a fashion creator
with one million subscribers.

14
00:00:52,522 --> 00:00:55,210
[1st generation fashion creator
who is still active after 10 years]

15
00:00:55,210 --> 00:00:59,079
I'm currently running a fashion platform
called KKST

16
00:00:59,079 --> 00:01:02,633
along with three fashion brands.

17
00:01:02,633 --> 00:01:04,475
[From casual and modern style]

18
00:01:04,475 --> 00:01:07,555
[To unique street fashion
that went to Seoul Fashion Week 2026 F/W]

19
00:01:07,555 --> 00:01:11,198
[A true fashion pioneer
spanning different genres]

20
00:01:11,198 --> 00:01:13,169
[A welcome sight at Ki Eunse's meeting,
Kkang Stylist]

21
00:01:13,169 --> 00:01:14,856
[At the interim rankings announcement]

22
00:01:14,856 --> 00:01:16,076
The gap is 140 million won.

23
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:17,295
From Indonesia.

24
00:01:17,295 --> 00:01:20,073
3rd-and 4th-place teams will catch up quickly.

25
00:01:20,073 --> 00:01:21,256
[170 million won gap
from Team China in 3rd place]

26
00:01:21,256 --> 00:01:22,633
Oh, the gap is small.

27
00:01:22,633 --> 00:01:25,413
[240 million won gap from 4th place]
We need to widen the gap drastically.

28
00:01:25,413 --> 00:01:27,028
Just one day can change the game.

29
00:01:27,028 --> 00:01:29,354
[Team Korea cannot rest easy]
We need to plan well for this.

30
00:01:29,354 --> 00:01:30,590
[Team Korea's Chat]

31
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,042
[Kkang, why don't we do a joint livestream
for clothing in Eunse's Findings?]

32
00:01:32,042 --> 00:01:34,053
[Sounds great!]
[Then let's do a meeting with a list of items!]

33
00:01:34,053 --> 00:01:36,490
[Ki Eunse initiating a joint livestream]

34
00:01:36,490 --> 00:01:39,459
We can drive more sales this way
than I can alone.

35
00:01:39,459 --> 00:01:42,948
Then it will naturally be more effective.

36
00:01:42,948 --> 00:01:46,566
We need to give one last push
to boost our sales.

37
00:01:46,566 --> 00:01:47,908
We need to claim first place.

38
00:01:47,908 --> 00:01:49,486
A joint livestream will give us synergy.

39
00:01:49,486 --> 00:01:51,320
The content will be more fun to watch.

40
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:54,645
We decided to do the joint streaming
expecting such benefits.

41
00:01:54,645 --> 00:01:57,142
I'm worried the sales won't be double
even if we do a joint streaming.

42
00:01:57,142 --> 00:01:58,579
[The final push of Team Korea]

43
00:01:58,579 --> 00:02:01,152
- Wow, there are a lot.
- I did bring many today.

44
00:02:01,152 --> 00:02:02,153
[Packed]
Hi. Hello.

45
00:02:02,153 --> 00:02:03,818
[Kkang Stylist came fully prepared]

46
00:02:03,818 --> 00:02:06,220
Aren't these shoes cute? They're nice.

47
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:08,867
- Oh, this must be your favorite piece.
- I restocked 4,000 pairs of them.

48
00:02:08,867 --> 00:02:12,748
[Shoes, bags, endless products are coming]
The first 2,000 pairs sold out in no time.

49
00:02:12,748 --> 00:02:14,669
In order of how well they're likely to sell.

50
00:02:14,669 --> 00:02:16,339
- Yes.
- Please list them.

51
00:02:16,339 --> 00:02:18,532
How much does a pair of those shoes cost?

52
00:02:18,532 --> 00:02:19,558
The retail price.

53
00:02:19,558 --> 00:02:21,352
We are selling at 1**, 000 won

54
00:02:21,352 --> 00:02:24,551
and the retail price is 1**, 000 won.

55
00:02:24,551 --> 00:02:26,753
[Hmm]

56
00:02:28,643 --> 00:02:30,321
[Reading the room]

57
00:02:30,321 --> 00:02:31,711
We can do 9*, 000 won.

58
00:02:31,711 --> 00:02:32,712
Oh, okay.

59
00:02:32,712 --> 00:02:33,989
[That's cute]

60
00:02:34,615 --> 00:02:38,904
You know, it made me feel a bit hesitant
to hear that it's over 100,000 won.

61
00:02:38,904 --> 00:02:41,314
[Discount rate is an important selling point]
I'd like to work on a couple of things.

62
00:02:41,314 --> 00:02:45,293
Please do tell.
It's the fastest that I decide on them here.

63
00:02:45,293 --> 00:02:48,757
[Negotiation skills activated as the show host]
Let's not do just one.

64
00:02:48,757 --> 00:02:51,766
[Nervous]

65
00:02:51,766 --> 00:02:54,238
Let's not do just one.

66
00:02:54,238 --> 00:02:56,437
It would be nice to have item six
in the 60,000-won range, too.

67
00:02:56,437 --> 00:02:57,638
- Which one?
- Item six.

68
00:02:57,638 --> 00:02:59,807
Like 69,000 won.

69
00:02:59,807 --> 00:03:01,576
Okay, 69,000 won.

70
00:03:01,576 --> 00:03:05,175
[Negotiation successfully done]
Okay, 69,000 won.

71
00:03:05,175 --> 00:03:06,572
We can decide on this quickly.

72
00:03:06,572 --> 00:03:07,758
The basic sweater.

73
00:03:07,758 --> 00:03:08,825
Basic sweater?

74
00:03:08,825 --> 00:03:10,418
In the 40,000-won range, maybe.

75
00:03:10,418 --> 00:03:13,387
[From the 60,000-to 40,000-won range?]
Oh, the cardigan?

76
00:03:13,387 --> 00:03:14,483
Okay.

77
00:03:14,483 --> 00:03:16,123
- Okay.
- Oh, is the 40,000-won range possible?

78
00:03:16,123 --> 00:03:17,944
Well, it's usually impossible.

79
00:03:17,944 --> 00:03:20,200
Then, 13*, 000 won for item ten?

80
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,201
[A rush of negotiation deals]

81
00:03:21,201 --> 00:03:22,243
Okay, sure.

82
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:24,685
If we could get item two's price
a little lower...

83
00:03:24,685 --> 00:03:26,697
- Okay.
- 19*, 000 won?

84
00:03:26,697 --> 00:03:28,543
- Yeah, that's possible.
- Wow, you're very generous.

85
00:03:28,543 --> 00:03:30,915
[Unending OK from the CEO]
Okay.

86
00:03:30,915 --> 00:03:32,600
- It's good that we're talking with the CEO.
- You're right.

87
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:34,744
The decisions are made directly.

88
00:03:34,744 --> 00:03:36,097
[Glancing]

89
00:03:36,097 --> 00:03:37,604
It's fine.

90
00:03:37,604 --> 00:03:38,819
[Shaking head]
The quantity is--

91
00:03:38,819 --> 00:03:40,320
[No idea how much he wants to sell]

92
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,682
She just shook her head.

93
00:03:41,682 --> 00:03:43,291
Okay, okay. 4*, 000 won.

94
00:03:43,291 --> 00:03:44,852
It sounds like there won't be much left
for you.

95
00:03:44,852 --> 00:03:47,798
That's okay.
We're investing in the relationship.

96
00:03:48,544 --> 00:03:50,756
[The investment]

97
00:03:50,756 --> 00:03:53,705
- We have one minute left, please be ready.
- It's hectic.

98
00:03:53,705 --> 00:03:55,897
- Cheer up.
- Cheer up!

99
00:03:55,897 --> 00:03:58,098
- Ready.
- I'll give you a cue.

100
00:03:58,098 --> 00:03:59,229
Go.

101
00:03:59,229 --> 00:04:01,107
- Welcome.
- Hello

102
00:04:01,107 --> 00:04:03,137
[The joint livestream starts]
Hello.

103
00:04:03,137 --> 00:04:07,416
Welcome back, everyone.
I'm here with a very special guest.

104
00:04:07,416 --> 00:04:08,631
[Ki Eunse leads the show smoothly]

105
00:04:08,631 --> 00:04:11,298
I'm the man who transforms people
through style, Kkang Stylist.

106
00:04:11,298 --> 00:04:13,016
[Kkang Stylist says hello shyly(?)]
Nice to meet you.

107
00:04:13,016 --> 00:04:14,398
[His ears turn red from nervousness]

108
00:04:14,398 --> 00:04:17,005
I posted my outfit of the day,

109
00:04:17,005 --> 00:04:19,973
and the reaction to the video was
something I've never seen before.

110
00:04:19,973 --> 00:04:21,114
The reaction was amazing.

111
00:04:21,114 --> 00:04:23,553
I received over 6,000 comments.

112
00:04:23,553 --> 00:04:24,554
Wow, 6,000?

113
00:04:24,554 --> 00:04:27,595
[Over 8,400 comments asking
for the information on the look]

114
00:04:27,595 --> 00:04:29,031
They're soft and drape beautifully.

115
00:04:29,031 --> 00:04:33,197
They're jeans. They're denim,
but they're so comfortable to wear.

116
00:04:33,197 --> 00:04:36,051
Even the waist is so comfortable.

117
00:04:36,051 --> 00:04:37,538
[Eunse is explaining about the product]
Around the belly.

118
00:04:37,538 --> 00:04:39,152
[But the CEO is just reacting to her?]
You're right.

119
00:04:39,152 --> 00:04:41,843
- I'll help her show you the jeans.
- Like this.

120
00:04:41,843 --> 00:04:44,390
- They also come in another color.
- The sneakers are pretty too.

121
00:04:44,390 --> 00:04:45,473
[Drawing breath]
They also come in another color.

122
00:04:45,473 --> 00:04:46,824
- The sneakers are pretty too.
- Right.

123
00:04:46,824 --> 00:04:48,287
- They're cute.
- Just like this.

124
00:04:48,287 --> 00:04:50,080
[Kkang Stylist missed his chance to jump in]
Look at this.

125
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:53,261
For casual summer shoes,
you have sneakers and athletic shoes.

126
00:04:53,261 --> 00:04:56,196
But it's hard to get that sophisticated look
with those shoes.

127
00:04:56,781 --> 00:04:57,809
[A joint livestream is not that easy]

128
00:04:57,809 --> 00:05:02,272
Since it was my first time livestreaming,
I was thinking about when I could jump in.

129
00:05:02,272 --> 00:05:04,321
I was supposed to support them in the show.

130
00:05:04,321 --> 00:05:07,224
But I didn't know how to jump in.

131
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:09,204
Eunse was leading the show so smoothly.

132
00:05:09,204 --> 00:05:11,007
I was worried I might interrupt the show.

133
00:05:11,007 --> 00:05:13,107
My head was filled with these thoughts.

134
00:05:13,107 --> 00:05:17,042
Kkang mostly did solo content so far.

135
00:05:17,042 --> 00:05:19,046
He seemed quite nervous.

136
00:05:19,046 --> 00:05:24,318
I think I put a lot of effort
into helping him loosen up.

137
00:05:24,318 --> 00:05:26,093
How does it look from a man's point of view?

138
00:05:26,093 --> 00:05:27,498
[Eunse inviting him to talk with a question]
If you're picking clothes for a wedding,

139
00:05:27,498 --> 00:05:30,620
[Kkang Stylist continuing the talk naturally]
This tweed jacket would be nice on top.

140
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:33,139
This is a must-have for spring.

141
00:05:33,139 --> 00:05:34,425
[Are you ready?]
Check out this firm, stretchy feel.

142
00:05:34,425 --> 00:05:36,355
[Message received]

143
00:05:36,355 --> 00:05:38,779
[Getting in sync]
Yes, it's a wool blend.

144
00:05:38,779 --> 00:05:43,252
[The joint livestream finding its rhythm]
Red and avocado are trending colors this S/S.

145
00:05:43,252 --> 00:05:44,989
Item 11 in navy is sold out?

146
00:05:44,989 --> 00:05:46,384
Oh, my...

147
00:05:46,384 --> 00:05:47,815
Oh, it's sold out in white.

148
00:05:47,815 --> 00:05:50,797
[Selling out one item after another]
Oh no, there will be nothing left for me.

149
00:05:50,797 --> 00:05:52,934
- What am I going to do if you buy them all?
- You are too late.

150
00:05:52,934 --> 00:05:55,889
[Meanwhile, as the two influencers race
toward a sellout...]

151
00:05:57,930 --> 00:06:00,712
[Beauty trendsetter with 17 years
of experience, Sangeununnie]

152
00:06:00,712 --> 00:06:03,391
[She greets someone politely]
Hello.

153
00:06:03,391 --> 00:06:05,990
- Hello. I'm Sangeununnie.
- Hello.

154
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:08,096
Let's start the unprecedented beauty war.

155
00:06:08,096 --> 00:06:11,159
[Sangeununnie going all in on the beauty war]
The unprecedented exclusive offers.

156
00:06:11,159 --> 00:06:15,825
I had to choose out of 150 brands

157
00:06:15,825 --> 00:06:18,405
and narrow down to nine.

158
00:06:18,405 --> 00:06:20,859
No matter which country I visit
or which cosmetics store I go to,

159
00:06:20,859 --> 00:06:24,648
I spend three to five million won on cosmetics
every time.

160
00:06:24,648 --> 00:06:28,652
I think of it as an investment in myself
and a way to learn.

161
00:06:28,652 --> 00:06:32,007
It's all about the product's quality.

162
00:06:32,007 --> 00:06:36,360
There's a bit of competition between brands
on the discount rate.

163
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:39,042
[Sangeununnie negotiating in person]
That's why I'm here myself.

164
00:06:41,295 --> 00:06:43,321
I looked up Gash on the internet,

165
00:06:43,321 --> 00:06:48,456
and the offer you gave me didn't seem
so different from your usual promotion.

166
00:06:48,456 --> 00:06:51,505
We'd like to win customers over
with the product rather than the price.

167
00:06:51,505 --> 00:06:54,959
See the forest, not the trees.

168
00:06:54,959 --> 00:06:57,044
I'm sure people will watch the broadcast

169
00:06:57,044 --> 00:06:59,013
and get curious about the product.
They will want to try out the product.

170
00:06:59,013 --> 00:07:01,816
[What she says is right] - Yes.
- Right.

171
00:07:01,816 --> 00:07:06,481
A lot of people in the beauty industry
will be watching.

172
00:07:06,481 --> 00:07:09,768
Can I share my opinion?

173
00:07:09,768 --> 00:07:11,726
[Of course]

174
00:07:11,726 --> 00:07:13,561
How about a 30% discount?

175
00:07:13,561 --> 00:07:14,582
30%?

176
00:07:14,582 --> 00:07:16,427
On Olive Young, we are--

177
00:07:16,427 --> 00:07:18,411
When I joined X THE LEAGUE,

178
00:07:18,411 --> 00:07:21,644
I declared war on Olive Young.
I told their manager I was sorry.

179
00:07:21,644 --> 00:07:23,725
This has to put the Olive Young sale to shame.

180
00:07:23,725 --> 00:07:26,106
The Olive Young sale happens every month.

181
00:07:26,106 --> 00:07:28,445
But this is a one-time-only chance with me.

182
00:07:28,445 --> 00:07:30,623
- You're right.
- She has a point.

183
00:07:30,623 --> 00:07:32,162
She does, indeed.

184
00:07:33,984 --> 00:07:36,617
[A perfect unarguable speech]

185
00:07:36,617 --> 00:07:38,477
Then, we can do...

186
00:07:39,119 --> 00:07:40,755
[Then?]
What we can do is

187
00:07:40,755 --> 00:07:44,198
35% off plus free shipping.

188
00:07:44,198 --> 00:07:46,193
Can we do 41%?

189
00:07:46,193 --> 00:07:50,464
How about we meet in the middle at 37%?

190
00:07:50,464 --> 00:07:52,920
- 37%.
- Oh well, under 40% is too low.

191
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:55,546
We went as far as a 7% increase.

192
00:07:55,546 --> 00:07:57,331
Also, there's free shipping.

193
00:07:57,331 --> 00:08:00,976
Then, for those who buy 6 types of products,

194
00:08:00,976 --> 00:08:03,757
[A full-size cleanser]
well, it could be this.

195
00:08:03,757 --> 00:08:06,374
[A full-size product as a free gift?]
Or a mini set as a gift?

196
00:08:06,374 --> 00:08:08,536
A couple of small facial mists could do, too.

197
00:08:08,536 --> 00:08:13,187
We can give a free cleanser
to the first customers who buy all six items.

198
00:08:13,187 --> 00:08:15,155
- First come, first served?
- Yes.

199
00:08:15,155 --> 00:08:16,889
- We can give some away to the first customers.
- Okay.

200
00:08:16,889 --> 00:08:18,854
- Because we never had a deal like this before.
- Yes, give it away.

201
00:08:18,854 --> 00:08:21,434
37% off for a 2-pack.

202
00:08:21,434 --> 00:08:24,979
Those who buy these four will get a makeup bag
and a mirror.

203
00:08:24,979 --> 00:08:26,611
- You said you'll give ten of these, right?
- Yes.

204
00:08:26,611 --> 00:08:27,636
- Yes.
- Yes.

205
00:08:27,636 --> 00:08:29,737
Great.

206
00:08:29,737 --> 00:08:31,134
[Sangeununnie's negotiation ended successfully]

207
00:08:31,134 --> 00:08:33,038
[Satisfied]
We have nothing left to give you.

208
00:08:33,038 --> 00:08:37,487
This 10-second bubble mask is one
of the most popular skincare products nowadays.

209
00:08:37,487 --> 00:08:39,456
I wouldn't miss this if I were you.

210
00:08:39,456 --> 00:08:41,281
The fourth product of the beauty war.

211
00:08:41,281 --> 00:08:43,109
The fifth product of the beauty war.

212
00:08:43,109 --> 00:08:44,709
The sixth product of the beauty war.

213
00:08:44,709 --> 00:08:45,753
The seventh product.

214
00:08:45,753 --> 00:08:46,790
The eighth product.

215
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:48,115
The last product is here.

216
00:08:48,115 --> 00:08:49,429
[The beauty war reaches its climax]
It's a body toner.

217
00:08:49,429 --> 00:08:51,063
The look gives off the successful CEO vibe.

218
00:08:51,063 --> 00:08:54,184
When tucked in, it creates a polished,
sophisticated spring look.

219
00:08:54,184 --> 00:08:58,218
[The race for No. 1, what will the result be?]
Guys, I got the deal for the stove.

220
00:08:59,267 --> 00:09:02,675
[Indonesia]

221
00:09:02,675 --> 00:09:04,203
[Team Indonesia from the first half of Round 1]

222
00:09:05,603 --> 00:09:10,311
[They had a conflict over lower sales
in the beginning]

223
00:09:10,311 --> 00:09:13,678
Then, how about we adjust the price?

224
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:17,068
Our people will definitely look
for something cheap.

225
00:09:17,651 --> 00:09:21,480
[A bold discount plan to revive sales begins]

226
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,896
How about 150,000 won?

227
00:09:22,896 --> 00:09:24,137
Okay!

228
00:09:24,137 --> 00:09:25,328
In addition to 150,000 won,

229
00:09:25,328 --> 00:09:28,122
how about we give a motorcycle
at a special price?

230
00:09:28,122 --> 00:09:30,620
[That's it]

231
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:33,547
[United to boost sales]

232
00:09:33,547 --> 00:09:35,450
- We need to be in the top 3, at least.
- Okay.

233
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:37,607
We need to be in the top 1, at least.

234
00:09:37,607 --> 00:09:39,566
[He can't be stopped]

235
00:09:41,862 --> 00:09:44,445
Our goal is to make Indonesia proud.

236
00:09:44,445 --> 00:09:48,100
We all share the same dream
of seeing Indonesia win.

237
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:50,952
But if we aren't having fun, we can't win.

238
00:09:50,952 --> 00:09:56,023
If Mami, Aurel, and Ashanty can all have fun,

239
00:09:56,023 --> 00:09:57,915
our team is definitely going to win.

240
00:09:57,915 --> 00:09:59,985
[Starting off with a joint livestream]

241
00:09:59,985 --> 00:10:08,076
[Each of them started selling
on their channels]

242
00:10:08,076 --> 00:10:09,804
[The result is?]

243
00:10:09,804 --> 00:10:11,997
Interim rankings for Round 1.

244
00:10:11,997 --> 00:10:13,841
First place goes to...

245
00:10:13,841 --> 00:10:14,897
Team Indonesia.

246
00:10:14,897 --> 00:10:17,902
[Team Indonesia takes first place
in the interim rankings]

247
00:10:17,902 --> 00:10:24,189
[Round 1 Interim Rankings No. 1
- Team Indonesia]

248
00:10:26,153 --> 00:10:29,047
Let's keep this up till the end.

249
00:10:29,047 --> 00:10:31,514
We will stick together, okay?

250
00:10:31,514 --> 00:10:33,232
But the gap is very small.

251
00:10:33,232 --> 00:10:34,340
It is very close.

252
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:36,434
- Oh.
- Oh my god.

253
00:10:37,298 --> 00:10:39,698
We're so proud to have taken first place.

254
00:10:39,698 --> 00:10:42,997
But at the same time, I am scared.

255
00:10:42,997 --> 00:10:47,225
Because the other countries are closing in.

256
00:10:47,909 --> 00:10:50,998
[First through fourth places separated
by only a small gap in sales]

257
00:10:50,998 --> 00:10:54,497
[What will be the sales strategy
of Team Indonesia to secure first place?]

258
00:10:54,497 --> 00:10:57,210
[Jakarta, Indonesia]

259
00:10:58,431 --> 00:11:01,174
[D-9 until the end of Round 1]

260
00:11:01,174 --> 00:11:03,708
[Ibnu and his crew gathered in a meeting room]

261
00:11:03,708 --> 00:11:05,324
[Indonesia's number one tech seller, Ibnu]
Now is our chance.

262
00:11:05,324 --> 00:11:07,210
It's Indonesia's chance to win.

263
00:11:07,946 --> 00:11:10,431
[Emphasizing again]
This is really important.

264
00:11:10,431 --> 00:11:13,779
We must win the first round.

265
00:11:13,779 --> 00:11:16,909
[Ibnu wants to hold on to first place]
What strategy should we go with?

266
00:11:16,909 --> 00:11:20,425
Looking at yesterday's sales,
I think this will do well.

267
00:11:20,425 --> 00:11:24,212
[Pricy smartphones are
the second-half strategy?]

268
00:11:24,212 --> 00:11:26,080
I'm a huge gadget freak.

269
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:29,117
When there's a new product,
I want to be the first one to use it.

270
00:11:29,117 --> 00:11:31,304
I'm the type who wants to get my hands
on those things first.

271
00:11:31,304 --> 00:11:33,920
So I thought maybe I could sell them myself.

272
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:35,901
[Ibnu is the No. 1 electronics seller]

273
00:11:36,944 --> 00:11:39,268
[Ibnu has made huge sales with electronics]

274
00:11:40,584 --> 00:11:43,506
[Ibnu pulls out his secret weapon]

275
00:11:43,506 --> 00:11:45,418
I'll give you a really special price.

276
00:11:45,418 --> 00:11:47,812
I'll give a little tip just for you.

277
00:11:50,569 --> 00:11:53,055
[Ibnu draws attention with a huge discount]

278
00:11:53,055 --> 00:11:56,853
Wait a moment. There are more reasons
why this phone is amazing.

279
00:11:59,562 --> 00:12:03,027
[He threw it?]

280
00:12:03,027 --> 00:12:08,319
[Ibnu's durability test shocks everyone on set]

281
00:12:08,319 --> 00:12:10,095
It's perfectly intact!

282
00:12:10,095 --> 00:12:13,561
Yes, this has incredible durability.

283
00:12:13,561 --> 00:12:16,467
[The next sales strategy to drive purchases
is setting a time limit]

284
00:12:16,467 --> 00:12:20,605
Three, two, one.

285
00:12:21,312 --> 00:12:25,251
[Encouraging quick purchases with a time limit]
Let's go.

286
00:12:28,561 --> 00:12:32,179
I want to give it my all to win.

287
00:12:32,179 --> 00:12:36,209
This is a special limited-time deal
exclusive to the first round of X THE LEAGUE.

288
00:12:36,209 --> 00:12:40,274
[A strategy to increase total sales at once]

289
00:12:40,904 --> 00:12:44,886
[Selling at a special price with a time limit]

290
00:12:44,886 --> 00:12:48,618
Take the chance right now! Hurry!

291
00:12:48,618 --> 00:12:49,619
[A timer is set here too]
Three.

292
00:12:49,619 --> 00:12:52,219
Two. One.

293
00:12:52,219 --> 00:12:55,262
Five, four, three.

294
00:12:55,262 --> 00:12:57,220
We're not just using a flash sale
as our strategy.

295
00:12:57,220 --> 00:13:00,441
All sales platforms in Indonesia have vouchers.

296
00:13:00,441 --> 00:13:06,465
The reason we set time limits of 10, 30 seconds
or a minute is to make sure

297
00:13:06,465 --> 00:13:09,238
customers don't miss out on the vouchers
and get discounted prices on the platforms

298
00:13:09,238 --> 00:13:12,448
so they receive all the benefits.

299
00:13:12,448 --> 00:13:17,491
Captain, the price is so good
it's already sold out.

300
00:13:17,491 --> 00:13:22,124
[All stock sold out!]

301
00:13:22,996 --> 00:13:26,851
I'll do my best, and I won't let anyone down.

302
00:13:26,851 --> 00:13:31,735
I really do hope
Indonesia becomes the ultimate winner.

303
00:13:34,262 --> 00:13:37,499
[Team Indonesia stepping up their selling game]

304
00:13:38,578 --> 00:13:42,391
[Will Team Indonesia be able to hold on
to first place?]

305
00:13:42,391 --> 00:13:44,754
[The fall of the two powerhouses]
They're like giants.

306
00:13:44,754 --> 00:13:47,263
The sheer size of the market is different.

307
00:13:47,263 --> 00:13:51,916
I thought it was over for us
because there's the USA and China.

308
00:13:51,916 --> 00:13:54,399
They're like the big boys.

309
00:13:54,399 --> 00:13:58,866
[China and USA expected to rank among the top]
China or the USA with the largest population

310
00:13:58,866 --> 00:14:01,487
must have an advantage in the competition.

311
00:14:01,487 --> 00:14:03,207
[However...]

312
00:14:03,207 --> 00:14:05,877
Third place is China.

313
00:14:06,541 --> 00:14:09,074
[Storytelling beauty seller]

314
00:14:10,992 --> 00:14:13,728
[K-Wanghong of 2.8 billion won monthly sales]
Wait, what?

315
00:14:13,728 --> 00:14:17,012
Gosh, this can't be right.

316
00:14:17,012 --> 00:14:21,122
The sales gap between third and fourth place
isn't that big.

317
00:14:21,122 --> 00:14:23,714
[There's only a 60 million won difference
between third and fourth place]

318
00:14:23,714 --> 00:14:27,580
We're not far ahead of the team
in fourth place.

319
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:30,398
They're only 60 million won behind us.

320
00:14:30,398 --> 00:14:33,301
We cannot let our guard down now.

321
00:14:33,301 --> 00:14:35,203
Third place is not low.

322
00:14:35,203 --> 00:14:38,830
But we came here aiming for first place.

323
00:14:38,830 --> 00:14:42,025
To be honest, our pride is hurt.

324
00:14:42,025 --> 00:14:45,802
But I think the real competition starts now.

325
00:14:45,802 --> 00:14:50,598
I'll put everything I've learned recently
to use for the remaining time.

326
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:53,400
The final result must be first place.

327
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:57,183
[Team China vows to turn things around
in the second half of the round]

328
00:14:57,183 --> 00:14:59,339
[Beijing, China]

329
00:15:00,122 --> 00:15:03,231
[D-8 until the end of Round 1]

330
00:15:03,231 --> 00:15:05,892
[Team China tries to step up their game
in the second half]

331
00:15:06,844 --> 00:15:08,836
[K-Wanghong of 2.8 billion won monthly sales,
Xiaoshu Ouni]

332
00:15:08,836 --> 00:15:14,567
I'm Xiaoshu Ouni, a Korean daughter-in-law
who married into a Chinese family.

333
00:15:14,567 --> 00:15:17,612
[At the first self-introduction]
Xiaoshu Ouni from Team China.

334
00:15:17,612 --> 00:15:22,216
Hello, I'm Lee Minseo from Korea.

335
00:15:22,216 --> 00:15:25,209
It's been six years
since I married my Chinese husband.

336
00:15:25,209 --> 00:15:30,191
I've been introducing Korean cosmetics
to China.

337
00:15:30,191 --> 00:15:35,239
In my opinion, livestream commerce
in China has evolved so much

338
00:15:35,239 --> 00:15:39,427
there's little room left for growth.

339
00:15:39,427 --> 00:15:40,428
That's the market now.

340
00:15:40,428 --> 00:15:43,647
Even those in rural or mountainous areas

341
00:15:43,647 --> 00:15:48,073
sell products by livestreaming on their phones.

342
00:15:48,073 --> 00:15:52,177
Livestream commerce is not just a way
of buying things.

343
00:15:52,177 --> 00:15:53,804
It's a way of living.

344
00:15:53,804 --> 00:15:56,956
I think that's China's advantage.

345
00:15:57,580 --> 00:16:02,154
[China's livestream commerce market is
highly competitive]

346
00:16:02,724 --> 00:16:07,464
[Xiaoshu Ouni works as a K-Wanghong
in a highly competitive market]

347
00:16:10,031 --> 00:16:14,168
When I'm livestreaming
I try all the skincare products on my face.

348
00:16:14,168 --> 00:16:17,271
Going on a livestream with makeup on
feels fake to me.

349
00:16:17,271 --> 00:16:21,871
Product tests feel more authentic
when I do them bare-faced.

350
00:16:21,871 --> 00:16:24,279
I don't put on any makeup while livestreaming.

351
00:16:24,279 --> 00:16:29,257
[Xiaoshu Ouni built trust and credibility
through bare-faced livestreams]

352
00:16:30,937 --> 00:16:32,991
[221,870,000 won in sales
from just one livestream]

353
00:16:32,991 --> 00:16:35,791
[224,550,000 won in sales on another day]

354
00:16:35,791 --> 00:16:39,705
[K-Wanghong with hundreds of millions in sales
from a single livestream]

355
00:16:43,142 --> 00:16:44,194
[Beep]

356
00:16:44,194 --> 00:16:45,899
Honey, honey.

357
00:16:45,899 --> 00:16:49,378
[A walkie-talkie at home?]

358
00:16:49,378 --> 00:16:52,005
Can you bring me a portable charger?

359
00:16:52,005 --> 00:16:55,109
The battery is low. The red light is on.

360
00:16:57,245 --> 00:16:59,284
Did you just wake up?

361
00:16:59,284 --> 00:17:03,187
[A man rushed over after hearing the call]

362
00:17:04,199 --> 00:17:08,256
You want me to introduce myself?

363
00:17:08,256 --> 00:17:11,416
I'm Xiaoshu's husband, Deng Qi.

364
00:17:11,416 --> 00:17:13,558
Since my wife
is so busy with her livestreaming,

365
00:17:13,558 --> 00:17:16,731
I help her around.

366
00:17:16,731 --> 00:17:18,452
[Why the walkie-talkie at home?]
Honey.

367
00:17:18,452 --> 00:17:21,769
We use the walkie-talkie
because our house is a bit too big.

368
00:17:21,769 --> 00:17:24,238
If I call him out loud, he can't hear me.

369
00:17:24,238 --> 00:17:28,231
It was also inefficient for me,
so we started carrying a walkie-talkie.

370
00:17:28,231 --> 00:17:30,507
We can reach each other faster than by phone.

371
00:17:30,507 --> 00:17:32,107
It's more efficient for us.

372
00:17:34,374 --> 00:17:36,984
[His look says it all]

373
00:17:36,984 --> 00:17:39,120
Honey!

374
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:40,180
What's up?

375
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:42,023
Why?

376
00:17:42,023 --> 00:17:43,423
I should go to her.

377
00:17:44,755 --> 00:17:47,054
[Climbing stairs non-stop at the wife's call]
Honey.

378
00:17:47,054 --> 00:17:49,112
Honey!

379
00:17:50,113 --> 00:17:54,310
If you have any favors to ask,
can you ask me all at once?

380
00:17:54,968 --> 00:17:56,504
I'm sorry.

381
00:17:56,504 --> 00:17:59,422
[Mission completed for wife]

382
00:17:59,422 --> 00:18:01,917
[Leaving without hesitation]
Bye.

383
00:18:03,902 --> 00:18:07,547
[What is she doing in bed
early in the morning?]

384
00:18:07,547 --> 00:18:10,390
Each chat has 500 members.

385
00:18:10,390 --> 00:18:12,986
I have 17 of them.

386
00:18:12,986 --> 00:18:16,555
After people purchase products
in my livestreams,

387
00:18:16,555 --> 00:18:18,838
they ask me about how to use those products
in the chat.

388
00:18:18,838 --> 00:18:21,392
They mostly consult with me
about their skin problems.

389
00:18:21,392 --> 00:18:24,187
Checking them is the first thing I do
in the morning.

390
00:18:24,187 --> 00:18:29,608
I reply to all feedback from customers
about the products I introduced.

391
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:32,326
[While she answers the inquiries
that piled up overnight]

392
00:18:33,409 --> 00:18:34,809
[Rattles]

393
00:18:35,514 --> 00:18:38,787
[Two men entering through the front door]

394
00:18:39,865 --> 00:18:40,896
[Rattles again]

395
00:18:41,848 --> 00:18:45,771
[Mysterious people entering
as if they live here]

396
00:18:47,230 --> 00:18:51,318
[Casually sitting in the living room
without the owner]

397
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:56,019
It must be unusual to see my employees coming
to work at my house.

398
00:18:56,837 --> 00:18:58,579
[Xiaoshu Ouni's home and office]

399
00:18:58,579 --> 00:19:02,077
To minimize the energy I put in,
I do livestreaming at home.

400
00:19:02,077 --> 00:19:06,282
All of my employees voluntarily moved
to places within a five-minute walk.

401
00:19:06,282 --> 00:19:11,181
I need to receive real-time reports
and analyze them during the livestream,

402
00:19:11,181 --> 00:19:16,611
I have traffic and operations teams ready,
and a video editing team working in real time.

403
00:19:16,611 --> 00:19:20,094
It's like a small livestream shopping.

404
00:19:20,801 --> 00:19:23,932
Let's review the last livestream first.

405
00:19:23,932 --> 00:19:27,235
[Xiaoshu Ouni's first livestream is coming up
after the interim rankings announcement]

406
00:19:27,235 --> 00:19:30,117
I'll begin with the basic data
from the recent livestream.

407
00:19:30,117 --> 00:19:31,634
We had 820,000 total views.

408
00:19:31,634 --> 00:19:35,751
The data was very stable,
and the conversion rate was also high.

409
00:19:35,751 --> 00:19:41,509
Then, can we prepare for potential questions
about today's products?

410
00:19:41,509 --> 00:19:43,720
People mostly ask about

411
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:47,148
how they are different
from what they've bought before.

412
00:19:47,148 --> 00:19:50,802
[Livestream analysis and anticipated questions]

413
00:19:52,294 --> 00:19:59,146
[Thorough preparation to rise in the rankings]

414
00:19:59,797 --> 00:20:01,279
[Livestream starts]

415
00:20:02,462 --> 00:20:04,798
[Starting the livestream bare-faced as usual]
Hi everyone, I'm back!

416
00:20:04,798 --> 00:20:07,286
Remember when I went to Cheongdam-dong
in Korea?

417
00:20:07,286 --> 00:20:10,599
I've prepared products dermatologists use.

418
00:20:10,599 --> 00:20:15,232
What is the special lineup I prepared
for today?

419
00:20:15,232 --> 00:20:17,771
Our toner is basically the same as a serum.

420
00:20:17,771 --> 00:20:21,381
And then our lotion.

421
00:20:21,381 --> 00:20:24,875
Use them together with a cream.
All three have a non-greasy texture.

422
00:20:24,875 --> 00:20:27,855
[A bundle deal to boost their ranking]

423
00:20:27,855 --> 00:20:31,624
It would be nice to increase the average
order value per customer a bit more.

424
00:20:32,318 --> 00:20:35,229
[Team China's strategy: Increase the AOV]
Okay. I'll do that.

425
00:20:35,229 --> 00:20:38,176
My strategy doesn't focus
on selling one product

426
00:20:38,176 --> 00:20:41,664
or selling different products at the same time.

427
00:20:41,664 --> 00:20:43,119
For example, within one brand,

428
00:20:43,119 --> 00:20:45,536
you use their facial mist and their sunscreen.

429
00:20:45,536 --> 00:20:48,427
And then you can have glowing and radiant skin
even without makeup.

430
00:20:48,427 --> 00:20:53,503
My strategy is building a skincare routine
like this within a brand.

431
00:20:53,503 --> 00:20:56,817
[Bundles to maximize the AOV]
Then people will buy the bundle.

432
00:20:56,817 --> 00:21:01,088
And that way,
I can dramatically increase total sales.

433
00:21:01,088 --> 00:21:04,271
My sales goal for Round 1 was

434
00:21:04,271 --> 00:21:07,608
six to eight million yuan.

435
00:21:07,608 --> 00:21:12,258
Since sales will determine the winner
in this round,

436
00:21:12,258 --> 00:21:16,482
I'm putting all my energy into this.

437
00:21:16,482 --> 00:21:19,997
I'm going to do my best to show what I can do.

438
00:21:22,083 --> 00:21:25,775
[Another beauty expert in Team China]

439
00:21:25,775 --> 00:21:27,118
He's just...

440
00:21:27,118 --> 00:21:32,762
At every single word he says,
I want to buy everything he has.

441
00:21:32,762 --> 00:21:35,445
[The mesmerizing seller acknowledged
by Guo Qing]

442
00:21:35,445 --> 00:21:37,431
[Storytelling beauty seller, Ran Gaoming]
Hello, I'm Ran Gaoming.

443
00:21:37,431 --> 00:21:43,196
I've been working as a livestream commerce
show host for four to five years now.

444
00:21:43,196 --> 00:21:49,793
I mainly specialize in
ingestible beauty and personal care products.

445
00:21:49,793 --> 00:21:51,223
[95 million won in sales]

446
00:21:52,133 --> 00:21:53,533
[100 million won in sales]

447
00:21:54,429 --> 00:21:55,927
[380 million won in sales]

448
00:21:55,927 --> 00:21:58,910
[Unmatched impact
generating hundreds of millions in sales]

449
00:21:58,910 --> 00:22:04,562
The room I mainly work in at home is
the bathroom.

450
00:22:04,562 --> 00:22:06,638
[Not the living room or bedroom,
but the bathroom is his main stage]

451
00:22:06,638 --> 00:22:10,376
[Beauty products filling every corner
of the bathroom]

452
00:22:10,376 --> 00:22:13,774
I spend one to two hours on skincare
in the bathroom.

453
00:22:13,774 --> 00:22:16,966
The bathroom is my secret base
where I get dolled up.

454
00:22:17,887 --> 00:22:20,955
A gentle friction and physical stimulation

455
00:22:20,955 --> 00:22:25,719
are way more effective in getting rid
of dead skin cells.

456
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:28,648
[Next step is moisturizing with a facial mist]

457
00:22:28,648 --> 00:22:31,077
The second step of the facial mist.

458
00:22:31,077 --> 00:22:34,169
[There are steps to using a facial mist?]
My eyes are probably my best feature.

459
00:22:34,169 --> 00:22:35,883
This is a mist for your eyeballs.

460
00:22:35,883 --> 00:22:39,786
[Hydrating not just the skin, but the eyes too]
Use it in the morning to steam and cleanse.

461
00:22:39,786 --> 00:22:43,058
If the whites of your eyes don't look clear
in the morning, give this a try.

462
00:22:43,058 --> 00:22:47,006
[Toner pad, facial mist, eyeball mist,
hair care, hair growing helmet]

463
00:22:47,006 --> 00:22:50,657
[Lash serum, eyebrow serum, recovery cream]

464
00:22:50,657 --> 00:22:55,335
[eye oil roller, lip balm]

465
00:22:55,335 --> 00:22:59,765
Skincare itself has a positive effect on me.

466
00:22:59,765 --> 00:23:04,779
Through consistent skincare,
I can pick out the best products.

467
00:23:04,779 --> 00:23:07,296
[In the living room now instead of bathroom?]

468
00:23:09,976 --> 00:23:14,057
I tested the products once more this morning.

469
00:23:14,057 --> 00:23:18,806
I'm confident in products that I test myself
and pick.

470
00:23:18,806 --> 00:23:22,676
[The first task of the day after skincare is
product testing]

471
00:23:22,676 --> 00:23:24,799
I don't like the smell.

472
00:23:24,799 --> 00:23:28,158
I cannot use a cosmetic product
if it smells bad.

473
00:23:28,158 --> 00:23:31,005
[Products that fail to meet strict standards
are eliminated without mercy]

474
00:23:31,005 --> 00:23:32,273
This is too sticky.

475
00:23:32,273 --> 00:23:34,836
It can't be this oily.

476
00:23:34,836 --> 00:23:35,985
[Eliminated items]

477
00:23:35,985 --> 00:23:38,005
[Only a few products pass his high standards]

478
00:23:38,005 --> 00:23:43,336
As for hydrating or moisturizing products
that deliver immediate results,

479
00:23:43,336 --> 00:23:45,266
you can really feel the difference.

480
00:23:45,266 --> 00:23:47,779
Body brightening lotion.

481
00:23:47,779 --> 00:23:49,257
I'll give it a moment and see how it absorbs.

482
00:23:49,257 --> 00:23:51,926
You're on hold for now.

483
00:23:51,926 --> 00:23:54,996
This is for treating skin breakouts
and improving complexion.

484
00:23:54,996 --> 00:23:57,616
I'll test this again in the evening.

485
00:23:58,264 --> 00:24:04,637
As for functional products, I keep them
in consideration and see how they perform.

486
00:24:04,637 --> 00:24:07,348
[A seller's eye for finding great products
through time and effort]

487
00:24:07,348 --> 00:24:11,399
What I sell is and has to be something
I have tested at home.

488
00:24:11,399 --> 00:24:15,415
That way,
I can say confidently that I sell what I use.

489
00:24:15,415 --> 00:24:18,403
[Only selling products proven
through his tests]

490
00:24:18,403 --> 00:24:19,803
It smells good.

491
00:24:21,072 --> 00:24:23,886
[Where is he headed after product testing?]

492
00:24:24,459 --> 00:24:27,660
I'll be selling two ingestible beauty products,

493
00:24:27,660 --> 00:24:30,754
a serum treatment, and a facial mask.

494
00:24:30,754 --> 00:24:35,535
What makes Korean skincare products special is
that they go beyond applying to your skin.

495
00:24:35,535 --> 00:24:38,342
They take care of your skin from within.

496
00:24:40,852 --> 00:24:43,112
[Ran Gaoming is rushing somewhere]

497
00:24:43,765 --> 00:24:46,702
Hello, can I ask you something?

498
00:24:46,702 --> 00:24:51,394
I'm a livestream commerce seller.
I brought a collagen supplement from Korea.

499
00:24:51,394 --> 00:24:54,552
I think women are more likely to take them.

500
00:24:54,552 --> 00:24:58,124
If I made you a collagen drink,
could you give it a try?

501
00:24:58,124 --> 00:24:59,177
[Nodding]

502
00:24:59,177 --> 00:25:01,930
[Hitting the streets for market research]
Thank you so much.

503
00:25:01,930 --> 00:25:03,696
[Puzzled]

504
00:25:03,696 --> 00:25:05,398
I took two straws.

505
00:25:05,398 --> 00:25:09,155
[How will Korean collagen be received locally?]
It's fine. No more stirring seems to be needed.

506
00:25:09,155 --> 00:25:10,474
Doesn't collagen taste fishy?

507
00:25:10,474 --> 00:25:15,386
It doesn't taste so fishy to me,
but what ladies think matters.

508
00:25:15,386 --> 00:25:18,778
[What will the customers think?]

509
00:25:20,146 --> 00:25:21,848
It doesn't taste fishy.

510
00:25:21,848 --> 00:25:24,917
It's fragrant,
just like a berry-flavored drink.

511
00:25:24,917 --> 00:25:26,855
What I drank before was really fishy.

512
00:25:26,855 --> 00:25:29,692
Does this drink taste okay for both of you?

513
00:25:29,692 --> 00:25:31,260
Yes, I love it.

514
00:25:32,733 --> 00:25:35,062
[After finishing market research]
Excuse me.

515
00:25:35,062 --> 00:25:38,841
Sorry to interrupt. I'm a live shopping seller.

516
00:25:38,841 --> 00:25:41,469
[Ran Gaoming accelerates sales for Round 1]

517
00:25:41,469 --> 00:25:44,972
[Products carefully selected
by testing them himself]

518
00:25:44,972 --> 00:25:50,144
My principle is simple regardless of the price
of the product.

519
00:25:50,144 --> 00:25:53,179
If I don't want to buy it,
I don't want to sell it.

520
00:25:53,179 --> 00:25:54,594
Only the products I am willing to buy
for myself

521
00:25:54,594 --> 00:25:56,656
are worth selling to you.

522
00:25:57,975 --> 00:26:01,526
[To uphold the honor of commerce powerhouse]

523
00:26:03,122 --> 00:26:07,729
[Team China continues their race till the end]

524
00:26:10,064 --> 00:26:12,127
Team USA ranked the lowest?

525
00:26:13,618 --> 00:26:18,957
[The result more shocking
than Team China ranking third]

526
00:26:18,957 --> 00:26:22,350
Eighth place is the United States.

527
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:24,635
[Team USA stuck at the bottom of the rankings]

528
00:26:28,315 --> 00:26:29,634
I don't think Team USA
has even started selling yet.

529
00:26:29,634 --> 00:26:30,986
- They haven't.
- You must be right.

530
00:26:30,986 --> 00:26:32,989
- This makes no sense.
- That number doesn't make sense.

531
00:26:32,989 --> 00:26:34,432
[Team USA's unbelievable ranking]

532
00:26:35,834 --> 00:26:38,588
[Team USA, speechless at the shocking result]

533
00:26:39,327 --> 00:26:43,912
We didn't do well in Round 1. That's for sure.

534
00:26:43,912 --> 00:26:46,699
No one from our team was excited about it.

535
00:26:46,699 --> 00:26:47,790
No.

536
00:26:47,790 --> 00:26:49,627
[A dismal eighth-place]

537
00:26:49,627 --> 00:26:51,258
There's no way.

538
00:26:52,826 --> 00:26:54,468
Oh, no.

539
00:26:54,468 --> 00:26:56,001
Not good.

540
00:26:56,001 --> 00:26:57,778
I was very disappointed.

541
00:26:57,778 --> 00:27:02,423
But it was because we didn't try hard enough.

542
00:27:02,423 --> 00:27:04,726
First place goes to Team USA.

543
00:27:04,726 --> 00:27:06,885
[From claiming first place
in the pre-match mission]

544
00:27:07,754 --> 00:27:13,006
[Team USA fell to eighth place
in the interim ranking announcement]

545
00:27:13,006 --> 00:27:17,010
Digital commerce in the US is much different
than commerce around the world.

546
00:27:17,921 --> 00:27:20,254
They can sell immediately on a livestream.

547
00:27:20,254 --> 00:27:23,070
Post once and sell instantly.

548
00:27:23,070 --> 00:27:27,441
American digital commerce has
a completely different way.

549
00:27:27,441 --> 00:27:30,376
Our audiences have to believe it's real.

550
00:27:30,376 --> 00:27:32,178
[American commerce culture values trust]
Because they get advertised to so much

551
00:27:32,178 --> 00:27:35,208
that they can tell what's real and what's not.

552
00:27:35,208 --> 00:27:39,689
I think it's important that everything fits
into what you were already doing.

553
00:27:39,689 --> 00:27:43,020
We're not going to create something
we've never done before

554
00:27:43,020 --> 00:27:47,135
or sell a product that doesn't feel organic
to what's already in your feed.

555
00:27:47,135 --> 00:27:48,780
Because obviously, it just won't sell.

556
00:27:48,780 --> 00:27:52,028
[Team USA's selling point is authenticity]
I think that's the number one thing.

557
00:27:52,028 --> 00:27:57,447
[Team USA building trust with content
where they use the actual product]

558
00:27:57,447 --> 00:27:58,991
When people see a product multiple times,

559
00:27:58,991 --> 00:28:02,524
they start to buy into the fact
that it's a product we believe in

560
00:28:02,524 --> 00:28:05,259
and that's something we use and finally buy it.

561
00:28:05,259 --> 00:28:08,843
I do believe we have a lot of room to grow.

562
00:28:09,418 --> 00:28:13,826
[Time to drive sales based on trust]

563
00:28:13,826 --> 00:28:17,889
Stormi is more of a traditional beauty model

564
00:28:17,889 --> 00:28:21,207
